Cloudron package patch: the first OIDC sign-in on an empty instance becomes
its owner and platform admin.

Opt-in with WARMBLY_OIDC_FIRST_USER_OWNER=true. While the instance still has
no accounts and the option is on, /v1/auth/config reports setup_required=false
so the login screen offers "Sign in with Cloudron" instead of redirecting to
the setup-link page, and cloudron_first_owner=true so the package's login
notice can say the first sign-in becomes the owner. The first account created by that OIDC sign-in receives
the same full admin grant as the upstream `warmblyctl setup-link` claim. The
grant runs under a Postgres advisory lock and only while no account holds any
admin permission, so a later or concurrent user can never become a second
owner. Apple, Google and password signups never take this path.

Until that first OIDC sign-in, the empty instance is reserved for it:
password, Apple and Google signups are refused and /v1/auth/config reports
registration closed, so nobody can create the first account ahead of the
owner. The setup link and warmblyctl do not use these gates and still work.

